<title>USA: BMW raises 1997 U.S. prices under one pct.</title>
<headline>BMW raises 1997 U.S. prices under one pct.</headline>
<dateline>WOODCLIFF LAKE, N.J. 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayerische Motren Werke AG's U.S. sales arm said it has raised 1997 U.S. model-year price by a volume-weighted average of less than one percent above 1996 prices.</p>
<p>BMW of North America Inc said the German luxury carmaker has added electronic all-season traction control as standard equipment to its entire U.S. model range for 1997. Previously, the system was a $1,100 option on selected models.</p>
<p>The automaker also said it is offering free scheduled maintenance work on all of its 1997 U.S. models for three years or 36,000 miles.  </p>
